IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc31-forms-periods`

-- ccc31-forms-soira.l4 -- Forms 52, 53 and 54 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: the Order To Comply with the Sex Offender
-- Information Registration Act, the Notice of Obligation To Comply with that Act, and the Obligation To Comply with it for an offence
-- identified as equivalent. Layer 1: the law as the Forms state it, from the text alone, from no one's point of view.
-- (Written by work/gen-soira.py, which keeps the three Forms in step; quotations are copied by srcrefs.py.)
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How to read a result (NOTES.md): MAYBE BOOLEAN. JUST TRUE: the notice's words reach the person. JUST FALSE: the notice says no in its own words
-- ("whenever required" not met, a period that has run, an "if" that fails). NOTHING: not covered (the person is not shown to be within the
-- notice, a seam answer is not JUST TRUE, or the notice is silent). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- The Sex Offender Information Registration Act is not among the sources: whether a person is "required under subsection 4(1) of that Act",
-- "under section 4.1 or 4.3" and the like are plain inputs. Whether an order is for life under s 490.013, 490.022 or 490.02904 is the answer
-- of the part that owns that section (`s 490.013(2)(c) ...` and so on; MAYBE BOOLEAN; NOTES.md "Seams").
-- A period "of ___ years after" a day is counted by ccc31-forms-periods: it begins ON the day named (fork F16).

§ `Form 52 (Section 490.012) -- Order To Comply with Sex Offender Information Registration Act`

-- src:19001 | FORM 52 (Section 490.012) Order To Comply with Sex Offender Information Registration Act
-- src:19002 | Canada,
-- src:19003 | Province of
-- src:19004 | (territorial division)
-- src:19005 | To A.B., of , (occupation), (address or address of court if no fixed address), (date of birth), (gender):
-- src:19006 | You have been convicted of or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for (description of offence(s)) under (applicable designated offence provision(s) of theCriminal Code), a designated offence (or designated offences) within the meaning of subsection 490.011(1) of the Criminal Code.
-- src:19007 | 1 You must report for the first time to the registration centre referred to in section 7.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, whenever required under subsection 4(1) of that Act.
-- src:19008 | 2 You must subsequently report to the registration centre referred to in section 7.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, whenever required under section 4.1 or 4.3 of that Act, for a period of years after this order is made (or if paragraph 490.013(2)(c) or any of subsections 490.013(3), (5) or (6) of the Criminal Code applies, for life).
-- src:19009 | 3 Information relating to you will be collected under sections 5 and 6 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act by a person who collects information at the registration centre.
-- src:19010 | 4 Information relating to you will be registered in a database, and may be consulted, disclosed and used in the circumstances set out in the Sex Offender Information Registration Act.
-- src:19011 | 5 If you believe that the information registered in the database contains an error or omission, you may ask a person who collects information at the registration centre referred to in section 7.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act or, if applicable, the Canadian Forces Provost Marshal, to correct the information.
-- src:19012 | 6 You have the right to apply to a court to terminate this order, and the right to appeal the decision of that court.
-- src:19013 | 7 If you are found to have contravened this order, you may be subject to a fine or imprisonment, or to both.
-- src:19014 | 8 If you are found to have provided false or misleading information, you may be subject to a fine or imprisonment, or to both.
-- src:19015 | Dated this day of , at .
-- src:19016 | (Signature of judge or clerk and name of court)
-- src:19017 | (Signature of person subject to order)
@ref Form 52 (Section 490.012) (src:19001-19017)
DECLARE `form 52 the period for which the person must report` IS ONE OF
    `form 52 for a period of years` HAS `form 52 the number of years` IS A NUMBER
    `form 52 for life`

-- "You have been convicted of or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for (description of offence(s)) under (applicable
-- designated offence provision(s) of the Criminal Code), a designated offence (or designated offences) within the meaning of subsection 490.011(1)."
@ref Form 52 (Section 490.012) (src:19006)
GIVEN `the person was convicted of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 490.011(1) the offence is a designated offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 52 the order applies to the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person was convicted of the offence` OR `the person was found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for the offence`)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "You have been convicted of or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder"
        IF `s 490.011(1) the offence is a designated offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "a designated offence (or designated offences) within the meaning of subsection 490.011(1) of the Criminal Code": the answer of s 490.011(1) is an input

-- Paragraph 1: "whenever required under subsection 4(1) of that Act": the "whenever" counts as "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (c)), so a person
-- not so required is JUST FALSE.
@ref Form 52 (Section 490.012) (src:19007)
GIVEN `the person is required to report for the first time under subsection 4(1) of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 52 para 1 the person must report for the first time` MEANS
    IF `the person is required to report for the first time under subsection 4(1) of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "You must report for the first time to the registration centre referred to in section 7.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, whenever required under subsection 4(1) of that Act"

-- Paragraph 2: "for a period of ___ years after this order is made (or if paragraph 490.013(2)(c) or any of subsections 490.013(3), (5) or (6) of the Criminal Code applies, for life)". A seam answering JUST TRUE for life makes the
-- period life; every seam answering JUST FALSE leaves the period of years; any other answer is NOTHING.
@ref Form 52 (Section 490.012) (src:19008)
GIVEN `the number of years the notice states` IS A NUMBER
      `s 490.013(2)(c) the order applies for life` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 490.013(3) the order applies for life` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 490.013(5) the order applies for life` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 490.013(6) the order applies for life` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE OF `form 52 the period for which the person must report`
`form 52 para 2 the period for which the person must report` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`s 490.013(2)(c) the order applies for life` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`s 490.013(3) the order applies for life` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`s 490.013(5) the order applies for life` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`s 490.013(6) the order applies for life` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            THEN JUST `form 52 for life`
        IF (`s 490.013(2)(c) the order applies for life` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`s 490.013(3) the order applies for life` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`s 490.013(5) the order applies for life` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`s 490.013(6) the order applies for life` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
            THEN JUST (`form 52 for a period of years` OF `the number of years the notice states`)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "if paragraph 490.013(2)(c) or any of subsections 490.013(3), (5) or (6) of the Criminal Code applies, for life": whether the order is for life is the answer of the part that owns section 490.013

-- Paragraph 2: must the person report on the day? "whenever required under section 4.1 or 4.3 of that Act" ("whenever" as "where": JUST FALSE if not
-- required) and within the period (a period the text fixes in its own words: outside it JUST FALSE, ruling (a) of 2026-11-05); for life, from the start.
@ref Form 52 (Section 490.012) (src:19008)
GIVEN period IS A `form 52 the period for which the person must report`
      `the day the order is made` IS A DATE
      `the person is required to report on the day asked about under section 4.1 or 4.3 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 52 para 2 the person must report on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is required to report on the day asked about under section 4.1 or 4.3 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "whenever required under section 4.1 or 4.3 of that Act"
        IF `the day asked about` LESS THAN `the day the order is made`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period of years after"
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER period
            WHEN `form 52 for a period of years` numberOfYears THEN
                IF `forms 24-54 the day falls within a period that begins on a day` `the day asked about` `the day the order is made` (`Length of time` OF numberOfYears, 0, 0, FALSE)
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period of years after"
            WHEN `form 52 for life` THEN JUST TRUE

@ref Form 52 (Section 490.012) (src:19009)
GIVEN `the person is subject to the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 52 para 3 information will be collected` MEANS
    IF `the person is subject to the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Information relating to you will be collected under sections 5 and 6 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act by a person who collects information at the registration centre": the notice speaks of the person it is given to

@ref Form 52 (Section 490.012) (src:19010)
GIVEN `the person is subject to the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 52 para 4 information will be registered` MEANS
    IF `the person is subject to the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Information relating to you will be registered in a database, and may be consulted, disclosed and used in the circumstances set out in the Sex Offender Information Registration Act": the notice speaks of the person it is given to

-- Paragraph 5: "If you believe that the information registered in the database contains an error or omission, you may ask ... to correct the information."
@ref Form 52 (Section 490.012) (src:19011)
GIVEN `the person is subject to the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person believes that the registered information contains an error or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 52 para 5 the person may ask for a correction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is subject to the order`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If you believe that the information registered in the database contains an error or omission, you may ask": the notice speaks of the person it is given to
        IF `the person believes that the registered information contains an error or omission`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If you believe that the information registered in the database contains an error or omission, you may ask"

@ref Form 52 (Section 490.012) (src:19012)
GIVEN `the person is subject to the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 52 para 6 the person may apply to terminate the order` MEANS
    IF `the person is subject to the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "You have the right to apply to a court to terminate this order": the right is that of the person the notice is given to

@ref Form 52 (Section 490.012) (src:19012)
GIVEN `the person is subject to the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court has decided an application to terminate the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 52 para 6 the person may appeal the decision` MEANS
    IF `the person is subject to the order` AND `a court has decided an application to terminate the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the right to appeal the decision of that court": the right is to appeal the decision of the court on the application

-- Paragraph 7: "If you are found to have contravened this order": JUST TRUE is "you may be subject to a fine or imprisonment, or to both" (a liability, not a certainty).
@ref Form 52 (Section 490.012) (src:19013)
GIVEN `the person is found to have contravened the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 52 para 7 the consequence of contravening the order` MEANS
    IF `the person is found to have contravened the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If you are found to have contravened this order"

-- Paragraph 8: "If you are found to have provided false or misleading information": JUST TRUE is "you may be subject to a fine or imprisonment, or to both" (a liability, not a certainty).
@ref Form 52 (Section 490.012) (src:19014)
GIVEN `the person is found to have provided false or misleading information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 52 para 8 the consequence of providing false or misleading information` MEANS
    IF `the person is found to have provided false or misleading information`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If you are found to have provided false or misleading information"

§ `Form 53 (Sections 490.019 and 490.032) -- Notice of Obligation To Comply with Sex Offender Information Registration Act`

-- src:19019 | FORM 53 (Sections 490.019 and 490.032) Notice of Obligation To Comply with Sex Offender Information Registration Act
-- src:19020 | Canada,
-- src:19021 | Province of ,
-- src:19022 | (territorial division).
-- src:19023 | To A.B., of , (occupation), a person referred to in subsection 490.02(1) of the Criminal Code:
-- src:19024 | Because, on (insert date(s)), you were convicted of, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for, (insert description of offence(s)), one or more offences referred to in paragraph (a), (c), (c.1), (d), (d.1) or (e) of the definition designated offence in subsection 490.011(1) of the Criminal Code or in paragraph (a) or (c) of the definition designated offence in section 227 of the National Defence Act, under (insert the applicable offence provision(s)), this is provided to give you notice that you are required to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act.
-- src:19025 | 1 You must report for the first time to the registration centre referred to in section 7.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, whenever required under subsection 4(2) of that Act.
-- src:19026 | 2 You must subsequently report to the registration centre referred to in section 7.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, whenever required under section 4.1 or 4.3 of that Act, for a period of years after you were sentenced, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, for the offence (or if paragraph 490.022(3)(c) or (d) of the Criminal Code applies, for life) or for any shorter period set out in subsection 490.022(2) of the Criminal Code.
-- src:19027 | 3 Information relating to you will be collected under sections 5 and 6 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act by a person who collects information at the registration centre.
-- src:19028 | 4 Information relating to you will be registered in a database, and may be consulted, disclosed and used in the circumstances set out in the Sex Offender Information Registration Act.
-- src:19029 | 5 If you believe that the information registered in the database contains an error or omission, you may ask a person who collects information at the registration centre referred to in section 7.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act or, if applicable, the Canadian Forces Provost Marshal, to correct the information.
-- src:19030 | 6 You have the right to apply to a court to exempt you from the obligation to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, and the right to appeal any decision of that court.
-- src:19031 | 7 You have the right to apply to a court to terminate the obligation, and the right to appeal any decision of that court.
-- src:19032 | 8 If you are found to have contravened the obligation, you may be subject to a fine or imprisonment, or to both.
-- src:19033 | 9 If you are found to have provided false or misleading information, you may be subject to a fine or imprisonment, or to both.
-- src:19034 | Dated this day of , at .
@ref Form 53 (Sections 490.019 and 490.032) (src:19019-19034)
DECLARE `form 53 the period for which the person must report` IS ONE OF
    `form 53 for a period of years` HAS `form 53 the number of years` IS A NUMBER
    `form 53 for life`

-- "Because, on (insert date(s)), you were convicted of, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for, (insert description of
-- offence(s)), one or more offences referred to in paragraph (a), (c), (c.1), (d), (d.1) or (e) of the definition designated offence in subsection 490.011(1)
-- of the Criminal Code or in paragraph (a) or (c) of the definition designated offence in section 227 of the National Defence Act ...
-- this is provided to give you notice that you are required to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act."
@ref Form 53 (Sections 490.019 and 490.032) (src:19024)
GIVEN `the person was convicted of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 490.011(1) the offence is referred to in paragraph (a), (c), (c.1), (d), (d.1) or (e) of the definition designated offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 227 of the National Defence Act the offence is referred to in paragraph (a) or (c) of the definition designated offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 53 the person is required to comply` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person was convicted of the offence` OR `the person was found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for the offence`)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Because, on (insert date(s)), you were convicted of, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for"
        IF (`s 490.011(1) the offence is referred to in paragraph (a), (c), (c.1), (d), (d.1) or (e) of the definition designated offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`s 227 of the National Defence Act the offence is referred to in paragraph (a) or (c) of the definition designated offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "one or more offences referred to in paragraph (a), (c), (c.1), (d), (d.1) or (e) of the definition designated offence in subsection 490.011(1) of the Criminal Code or in paragraph (a) or (c) of the definition designated offence in section 227 of the National Defence Act": the answers of s 490.011(1) and of the National Defence Act are inputs

-- Paragraph 1: "whenever required under subsection 4(2) of that Act": the "whenever" counts as "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (c)), so a person
-- not so required is JUST FALSE.
@ref Form 53 (Sections 490.019 and 490.032) (src:19025)
GIVEN `the person is required to report for the first time under subsection 4(2) of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 53 para 1 the person must report for the first time` MEANS
    IF `the person is required to report for the first time under subsection 4(2) of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "You must report for the first time to the registration centre referred to in section 7.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, whenever required under subsection 4(2) of that Act"

-- Paragraph 2: "for a period of ___ years after you were sentenced, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, for the offence (or if paragraph 490.022(3)(c) or (d) of the Criminal Code applies, for life) or for any shorter period set out in subsection 490.022(2) of the Criminal Code". A seam answering JUST TRUE for life makes the
-- period life; every seam answering JUST FALSE leaves the period of years (the shorter period set out in subsection 490.022(2), if it is shorter, takes its place); any other answer is NOTHING.
@ref Form 53 (Sections 490.019 and 490.032) (src:19026)
GIVEN `the number of years the notice states` IS A NUMBER
      `s 490.022(3)(c) the obligation applies for life` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 490.022(3)(d) the obligation applies for life` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a shorter period applies under subsection 490.022(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shorter period in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE OF `form 53 the period for which the person must report`
`form 53 para 2 the period for which the person must report` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`s 490.022(3)(c) the obligation applies for life` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`s 490.022(3)(d) the obligation applies for life` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            THEN JUST `form 53 for life`
        IF (`s 490.022(3)(c) the obligation applies for life` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`s 490.022(3)(d) the obligation applies for life` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND `a shorter period applies under subsection 490.022(2)` AND `the shorter period in years` LESS THAN `the number of years the notice states`
            THEN JUST (`form 53 for a period of years` OF `the shorter period in years`)
        IF (`s 490.022(3)(c) the obligation applies for life` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`s 490.022(3)(d) the obligation applies for life` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
            THEN JUST (`form 53 for a period of years` OF `the number of years the notice states`)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "if paragraph 490.022(3)(c) or (d) of the Criminal Code applies, for life": whether the order is for life is the answer of the part that owns section 490.022

-- Paragraph 2: must the person report on the day? "whenever required under section 4.1 or 4.3 of that Act" ("whenever" as "where": JUST FALSE if not
-- required) and within the period (a period the text fixes in its own words: outside it JUST FALSE, ruling (a) of 2026-11-05); for life, from the start.
@ref Form 53 (Sections 490.019 and 490.032) (src:19026)
GIVEN period IS A `form 53 the period for which the person must report`
      `the day the person was sentenced or found not criminally responsible` IS A DATE
      `the person is required to report on the day asked about under section 4.1 or 4.3 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 53 para 2 the person must report on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is required to report on the day asked about under section 4.1 or 4.3 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "whenever required under section 4.1 or 4.3 of that Act"
        IF `the day asked about` LESS THAN `the day the person was sentenced or found not criminally responsible`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period of years after"
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER period
            WHEN `form 53 for a period of years` numberOfYears THEN
                IF `forms 24-54 the day falls within a period that begins on a day` `the day asked about` `the day the person was sentenced or found not criminally responsible` (`Length of time` OF numberOfYears, 0, 0, FALSE)
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period of years after"
            WHEN `form 53 for life` THEN JUST TRUE

