§ `Form 54 (Sections 490.02901 to 490.02903, 490.02905 and 490.032) -- Obligation To Comply with Sex Offender Information Registration Act`

-- src:19036 | FORM 54 (Sections 490.02901 to 490.02903, 490.02905 and 490.032) Obligation To Comply with Sex Offender Information Registration Act
-- src:19037 | To A.B., of , (occupation), (address in Canada), (date of birth), (gender):
-- src:19038 | Because, on (date), you were convicted of or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for an offence (or offences) in (location of offence(s)) that the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, has identified as being equivalent to (description of offence(s)) under (applicable provision(s) of theCriminal Code), an offence (or offences) referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition primary offence in subsection 490.011(1) of the Criminal Code;
-- src:19039 | You are provided with this to inform you that you are required to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act.
-- src:19040 | 1 You must report for the first time to the registration centre referred to in section 7.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, whenever required under subsection 4(2) of that Act.
-- src:19041 | 2 You must subsequently report to the registration centre referred to in section 7.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, whenever required under section 4.1 or 4.3 of that Act, for a period of years after the day on which you were sentenced or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for the offence (or if paragraph 490.02904(3)(c) or (d) of the Criminal Code applies, for life because you were convicted of or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for an offence (or offences) that the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, has identified as equivalent to (description of offence(s)) under (applicable offence provision(s) of theCriminal Code), an offence (or offences) referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition primary offence in subsection 490.011(1) of the Criminal Code) or for any shorter period determined under subsection 490.02904(2) of the Criminal Code.
-- src:19042 | 3 Information relating to you will be collected under sections 5 and 6 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act by a person who collects information at the registration centre.
-- src:19043 | 4 Information relating to you will be registered in a database, and may be consulted, disclosed and used in the circumstances set out in the Sex Offender Information Registration Act.
-- src:19044 | 5 If you believe that the information registered in the database contains an error or omission, you may ask a person who collects information at the registration centre referred to in section 7.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act to correct the information.
-- src:19045 | 6 You have the right to apply to a court to exempt you from the obligation to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, and the right to appeal the decision of that court.
-- src:19046 | 6.1 You have the right to apply to a court to vary the duration of the obligation to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act if the obligation applies for life because you were convicted or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for more than one offence, and you have the right to appeal the decision of that court.
-- src:19047 | 7 You have the right to apply to a court to terminate the obligation to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act and the right to appeal the decision of that court.
-- src:19048 | 8 If you are found to have not complied with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, you may be subject to a fine or imprisonment, or to both.
-- src:19049 | 9 If you are found to have provided false or misleading information, you may be subject to a fine or imprisonment, or to both.
-- src:19050 | Served on (date).
-- src:19051 | For administrative use only:
-- src:19052 | Sentence imposed or verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder rendered on (date).
@ref Form 54 (Sections 490.02901 to 490.02903, 490.02905 and 490.032) (src:19036-19052)
DECLARE `form 54 the period for which the person must report` IS ONE OF
    `form 54 for a period of years` HAS `form 54 the number of years` IS A NUMBER
    `form 54 for life`

-- "Because, on (date), you were convicted of or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for an offence (or offences) in (location of
-- offence(s)) that the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, has identified as being equivalent to (description of
-- offence(s)) ..., an offence (or offences) referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition primary offence in subsection 490.011(1) ... You are provided with
-- this to inform you that you are required to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act."
@ref Form 54 (Sections 490.02901 to 490.02903, 490.02905 and 490.032) (src:19038-19039)
GIVEN `the person was convicted of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General of the province or the minister of justice of the territory has identified the offence as equivalent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 490.011(1) the equivalent offence is referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition primary offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 54 the person is required to comply` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person was convicted of the offence` OR `the person was found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for the offence`)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Because, on (date), you were convicted of or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for an offence"
        IF NOT `the Attorney General of the province or the minister of justice of the territory has identified the offence as equivalent`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, has identified as being equivalent to"
        IF `s 490.011(1) the equivalent offence is referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition primary offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "an offence (or offences) referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition primary offence in subsection 490.011(1) of the Criminal Code": the answer of s 490.011(1) is an input

-- Paragraph 1: "whenever required under subsection 4(2) of that Act": the "whenever" counts as "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (c)), so a person
-- not so required is JUST FALSE.
@ref Form 54 (Sections 490.02901 to 490.02903, 490.02905 and 490.032) (src:19040)
GIVEN `the person is required to report for the first time under subsection 4(2) of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 54 para 1 the person must report for the first time` MEANS
    IF `the person is required to report for the first time under subsection 4(2) of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "You must report for the first time to the registration centre referred to in section 7.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, whenever required under subsection 4(2) of that Act"

-- Paragraph 2: "for a period of ___ years after the day on which you were sentenced or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for the offence (or if paragraph 490.02904(3)(c) or (d) of the Criminal Code applies, for life) or for any shorter period determined under subsection 490.02904(2) of the Criminal Code". A seam answering JUST TRUE for life makes the
-- period life; every seam answering JUST FALSE leaves the period of years (the shorter period determined under subsection 490.02904(2), if it is shorter, takes its place); any other answer is NOTHING.
@ref Form 54 (Sections 490.02901 to 490.02903, 490.02905 and 490.032) (src:19041)
GIVEN `the number of years the notice states` IS A NUMBER
      `s 490.02904(3)(c) the obligation applies for life` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 490.02904(3)(d) the obligation applies for life` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a shorter period applies under subsection 490.02904(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shorter period in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE OF `form 54 the period for which the person must report`
`form 54 para 2 the period for which the person must report` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`s 490.02904(3)(c) the obligation applies for life` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`s 490.02904(3)(d) the obligation applies for life` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            THEN JUST `form 54 for life`
        IF (`s 490.02904(3)(c) the obligation applies for life` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`s 490.02904(3)(d) the obligation applies for life` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND `a shorter period applies under subsection 490.02904(2)` AND `the shorter period in years` LESS THAN `the number of years the notice states`
            THEN JUST (`form 54 for a period of years` OF `the shorter period in years`)
        IF (`s 490.02904(3)(c) the obligation applies for life` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`s 490.02904(3)(d) the obligation applies for life` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
            THEN JUST (`form 54 for a period of years` OF `the number of years the notice states`)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "if paragraph 490.02904(3)(c) or (d) of the Criminal Code applies, for life": whether the order is for life is the answer of the part that owns section 490.02904

-- Paragraph 2: must the person report on the day? "whenever required under section 4.1 or 4.3 of that Act" ("whenever" as "where": JUST FALSE if not
-- required) and within the period (a period the text fixes in its own words: outside it JUST FALSE, ruling (a) of 2026-11-05); for life, from the start.
@ref Form 54 (Sections 490.02901 to 490.02903, 490.02905 and 490.032) (src:19041)
GIVEN period IS A `form 54 the period for which the person must report`
      `the day the person was sentenced or found not criminally responsible` IS A DATE
      `the person is required to report on the day asked about under section 4.1 or 4.3 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 54 para 2 the person must report on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is required to report on the day asked about under section 4.1 or 4.3 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "whenever required under section 4.1 or 4.3 of that Act"
        IF `the day asked about` LESS THAN `the day the person was sentenced or found not criminally responsible`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period of years after"
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER period
            WHEN `form 54 for a period of years` numberOfYears THEN
                IF `forms 24-54 the day falls within a period that begins on a day` `the day asked about` `the day the person was sentenced or found not criminally responsible` (`Length of time` OF numberOfYears, 0, 0, FALSE)
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period of years after"
            WHEN `form 54 for life` THEN JUST TRUE

@ref Form 54 (Sections 490.02901 to 490.02903, 490.02905 and 490.032) (src:19042)
GIVEN `the person is subject to the obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 54 para 3 information will be collected` MEANS
    IF `the person is subject to the obligation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Information relating to you will be collected under sections 5 and 6 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act by a person who collects information at the registration centre": the notice speaks of the person it is given to

@ref Form 54 (Sections 490.02901 to 490.02903, 490.02905 and 490.032) (src:19043)
GIVEN `the person is subject to the obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 54 para 4 information will be registered` MEANS
    IF `the person is subject to the obligation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Information relating to you will be registered in a database, and may be consulted, disclosed and used in the circumstances set out in the Sex Offender Information Registration Act": the notice speaks of the person it is given to

-- Paragraph 5: "If you believe that the information registered in the database contains an error or omission, you may ask ... to correct the information."
@ref Form 54 (Sections 490.02901 to 490.02903, 490.02905 and 490.032) (src:19044)
GIVEN `the person is subject to the obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person believes that the registered information contains an error or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 54 para 5 the person may ask for a correction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is subject to the obligation`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If you believe that the information registered in the database contains an error or omission, you may ask": the notice speaks of the person it is given to
        IF `the person believes that the registered information contains an error or omission`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If you believe that the information registered in the database contains an error or omission, you may ask"

@ref Form 54 (Sections 490.02901 to 490.02903, 490.02905 and 490.032) (src:19045)
GIVEN `the person is subject to the obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 54 para 6 the person may apply for an exemption` MEANS
    IF `the person is subject to the obligation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "You have the right to apply to a court to exempt you from the obligation to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act": the right is that of the person the notice is given to

@ref Form 54 (Sections 490.02901 to 490.02903, 490.02905 and 490.032) (src:19045)
GIVEN `the person is subject to the obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court has decided an application for an exemption` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 54 para 6 the person may appeal the decision on the exemption` MEANS
    IF `the person is subject to the obligation` AND `a court has decided an application for an exemption`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the right to appeal the decision of that court": the right is to appeal the decision of the court on the application

@ref Form 54 (Sections 490.02901 to 490.02903, 490.02905 and 490.032) (src:19047)
GIVEN `the person is subject to the obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 54 para 7 the person may apply to terminate the obligation` MEANS
    IF `the person is subject to the obligation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "You have the right to apply to a court to terminate the obligation to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act": the right is that of the person the notice is given to

@ref Form 54 (Sections 490.02901 to 490.02903, 490.02905 and 490.032) (src:19047)
GIVEN `the person is subject to the obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court has decided an application to terminate the obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 54 para 7 the person may appeal the decision on termination` MEANS
    IF `the person is subject to the obligation` AND `a court has decided an application to terminate the obligation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the right to appeal the decision of that court": the right is to appeal the decision of the court on the application

-- Paragraph 8: "If you are found to have not complied with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act": JUST TRUE is "you may be subject to a fine or imprisonment, or to both" (a liability, not a certainty).
@ref Form 54 (Sections 490.02901 to 490.02903, 490.02905 and 490.032) (src:19048)
GIVEN `the person is found to have not complied with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 54 para 8 the consequence of not complying` MEANS
    IF `the person is found to have not complied with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If you are found to have not complied with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act"

-- Paragraph 9: "If you are found to have provided false or misleading information": JUST TRUE is "you may be subject to a fine or imprisonment, or to both" (a liability, not a certainty).
@ref Form 54 (Sections 490.02901 to 490.02903, 490.02905 and 490.032) (src:19049)
GIVEN `the person is found to have provided false or misleading information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 54 para 9 the consequence of providing false or misleading information` MEANS
    IF `the person is found to have provided false or misleading information`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If you are found to have provided false or misleading information"

-- Paragraph 6.1: "You have the right to apply to a court to vary the duration of the obligation ... if the obligation applies for life because you were
-- convicted or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for more than one offence, and you have the right to appeal the decision of that court."
@ref Form 54 (Sections 490.02901 to 490.02903, 490.02905 and 490.032) (src:19046)
